docs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Converter scratch
*.canonical.ply

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# NOTE: data/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
# The player and the .sog frames are served from the SAME public repo so
# everything is same-origin on GitHub Pages and no CORS config is needed.
# The frames are committed via Git.
#
# Before committing a full sequence, check the converter's summary:
#   - each .sog must stay under the 100 MB per-file push limit
#   - the total must stay under the ~1 GB Pages published-site ceiling
# Reduce with --frame-step or --sh-degree if not. Do NOT reach for Git LFS
# first: GitHub Pages has historically not served LFS objects directly.
#
# Re-converting a sequence at a lower frame-step leaves orphaned frames from
# the previous run. They are not in any manifest, so the converter's size
# report does not count them — but Git would commit them permanently.
# Check on-disk vs manifest frame counts before the first commit.

# --- Which sequences ship in the repo -------------------------------------
# Frames are excluded by default and allowed back in per sequence. Everything
# else under data/ — manifest.json and index.json — stays tracked regardless,
# so the library, its cameras and its backgrounds remain version-controlled
# even for sequences whose frames live in object storage.
#
# To publish a sequence with the site, add a negation for it below and clear
# its baseUrl:  py tools/set_host.py <name> --local
data/*/frame_*.sog
!data/bogdanFly/frame_*.sog
